# Local browser links (mandatory in agent replies)

Whenever you mention a path under `modules/` or `scripts/` — summaries, audits, PR test plans, verification tables, not only defects — provide a **markdown link** with base `http://localhost/it-management/` and tell the user to **open it in a new browser tab**.

## URL patterns

| Path | URL |
|------|-----|
| Module page | `http://localhost/it-management/modules/<slug>/<file>.php` |
| Script landing | `http://localhost/it-management/scripts/<file>.php?run=1` |
| Script apply flow | `…?run=1&apply=1` (Admin) |
| No-auth plain probe | `http://localhost/it-management/scripts/<file>.php` (omit `run=1` when script is no-auth, e.g. `count_db_tables.php`) |

Note **Admin session** when required, or **no login** for no-auth scripts. Multi-row lists need a link per script/module — do not cite bare repo paths without a localhost URL.

## Examples

- [Open modules/hotel_bookings/index.php](http://localhost/it-management/modules/hotel_bookings/index.php)
- [verify_command_palette_sidebar_slugs.php?run=1](http://localhost/it-management/scripts/verify_command_palette_sidebar_slugs.php?run=1)
- [scripts/scripts.php catalog](http://localhost/it-management/scripts/scripts.php?run=1)

See `AGENTS.md` step **7a** for the full contract.
